WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.868
-Welcome, welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.601
You're here.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:06.801
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.834
What a great day
it was today, guys.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.300
Compared to yesterday,
didn't New York City

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.467
seem so quiet today?

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:17.267
It felt like going from
a TJ Maxx to a library.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.868
You know,
didn't it a little bit?

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.601
Yup, yesterday was crazy
because former President Trump

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:24.267
got arrested here
in New York City, and...

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:26.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:30.667
...the news covered every move,
his every, every move.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.901
But most of it was
just him traveling.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.234
Did you see?
I'm not sure

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.501
we needed a play by play
of a guy's trip to the airport.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.067
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.567
It was like Trump clicked
Share my Uber trip

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:42.901
with the entire country.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:46.434
Yep, the news literally covered
Trump's rides to the airport.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.300
The only time I care about
someone getting to the airport

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.767
is my uncle after Thanksgiving.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:50.968
Alright, he's on the plane.
Go.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.634
Thank you, bye.

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:55.133
Thank you so much.
Yep.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.701
Trump is facing
34 felony counts

00:00:57.701 --> 00:00:59.701
because of hush money payments
he made to porn star

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:03.968
Stormy Daniels and Playboy
model Karen McDougal.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.901
But get this, Trump also
reportedly paid off a doorman

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.367
who claimed to know about a
secret child he fathered.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.000
-Ooh.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.100
-So Trump paid hush money
to a porn star,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.767
a Playboy model
and secretly fathered a child.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.234
He sounds less like
the former president

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:19.133
and more like a former
member of Motley Crue.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.968
The doorman,
the doorman got suspicious

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.901
at a Trump Tower birthday party
when the kid fired the magician.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:29.067
"You're fired."
And he go, "Wait.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.534
You...

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.000
Where do you live?"

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:39.167
Of course, Trump denies
secretly fathering a child.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.400
He was like, "Technically,
I've never fathered any child."

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.934
Send the butler down to
Don Jr.'s baseball game.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.167
Well, there weren't any video
cameras in the courtroom

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:54.367
during Trump's arraignment, but
there were some sketch artists.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.000
Here's one of
their drawings here.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.167
Ooh.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.801
Of course, the courtroom sketch
is sponsored by Velveeta.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.067
Meanwhile, Trump didn't
take a mug shot,

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.334
but his campaign is already
selling t-shirts

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:11.901
with a fake mug shot on them.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.033
And this is -- this is real.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.934
They added two inches
to Trump's height

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.200
to make him 6'5."

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.167
Check this out.
This is real, yeah.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:21.767
Then Stormy Daniels said,

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.267
"Well, you got
the two inches part, right?"

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:24.601
Hey, whoa, wait.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.067
-Whoa!
-"You're fired!"

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.300
"Alright."

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.400
I heard that the judge
overseeing Trump's case

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.601
has set the next
in-person hearing for December,

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.434
and Stormy Daniels
may be there.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:42.601
[ Audiences "Oohs" ]

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:44.300
And in honor
of Stormy Daniels being there,

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.400
Lexus is already planning
their awkward December

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.200
to remember sales event.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.934
Meanwhile,
after his arraignment,

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.501
Trump flew back home
to Florida

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.701
and held a rally in Mar-a-Lago.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.100
It's always nice to have
a traditional

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.667
post-arrest reception.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.868
The whole staff looked
at him like, "Back so soon?"

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:04.934
Switching gears, listen to this.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.734
In a new documentary,
Pope Francis

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:10.567
said that sex
is a beautiful thing.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:13.300
That's because he's only seen it
in Renaissance oil paintings.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:19.934
It was even weirder because
the question was,

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.234
have you thought
about retiring?

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.834
It had nothing to do...

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.234
Some big movie news today.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.067
Nintendo's
"Super Mario Bros. Movie"

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.534
finally hit theaters.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:31.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.901
And of course, with this movie,
if you're a younger sibling,

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.801
you have to watch
your big brother watch it first.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.767
There you go, guys.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.267
Finally, it is Wednesday night.
And you know what that means.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:43.067
It's "Tonight Show" Audience
trivia Night.

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:50.300
-♪ Tonight audience
trivia night ♪

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.400
-Now, I'm going to
ask random people

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.200
in the audience
a trivia question.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.300
And if you answer correctly,
you win a prize.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.834
Who wants to play?
Anyone want to play?

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:00.334
No one on this side
wants to play?

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.400
Right over here, come here.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.634
Oh, yeah.
Hey, here you go.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:05.734
Ready? What is your name?
-Ella.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.601
-Ella, where are you from?
-California.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:09.634
-Hey. Welcome, Ella,
from California.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:12.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.801
-Alright, here's the question.

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:19.901
-Seconds?

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.667
Milliseconds?

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.334
-Judges.
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:24.434
-Sorry.
The answer was...

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.434
Sorry. Thank you so much.
Thank you for playing.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.567
Who else wants to play?

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.434
Yeah, right there, buddy.
Hey, there you go.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.267
Here you go. What's your name
and where are you from?

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.467
-Michael from Texas.
-Michael from Texas!

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:36.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:38.367
-Come on, Texas.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.000
-Texas, alright.
Here's the question.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.534
-Oh, I don't know.

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:48.934
The one down?

00:04:48.934 --> 00:04:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.868
-The one down. Judges?
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:54.634
I'm sorry.
It's Ozempic.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.133
Ozempic. Thank you so much.
How about -- who else?

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.400
Anyone over here?
Yes. Hey, bud.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.200
How you doing? That's for you.
-How are you?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.968
-That's a great shirt.
-Thank you.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:05.033
What is your name?
Where are you from?

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.534
-Corey,
from Detroit, Michigan.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.200
-Yeah, Detroit.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.334
Alright, here we go.

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:19.334
-Frostbite?

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:20.601
-Judges?
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:22.734
No, skiing with Gwyneth Paltrow.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:24.100
Thank you so much.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.167
Thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:26.501
Let me -- let's go around here.

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:29.934
I'll go around.
I'll go around this side.

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:32.300
Hey, how are you guys doing?
Doing good, looking good.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.267
Good looking audience.
Hey, bud.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.701
Get up, get up!
Stand, hey.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.200
What's your name?
-Loic.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.601
-Louie?
-Loic. French. French name.

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:41.667
-Loic?
-Yeah.

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:43.934
-Well, Loic from France.

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:45.667
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:46.901
-Here you go, hold that.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.234
I'll give you the question here.
Ready, Loic?

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:55.767
-Whoa.
-What agency monitors

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:59.567
the activities of all Americans?

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:02.400
-The government?
Yeah.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.634
-Government?
[ Buzzer ]

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:05.267
Ah, TikTok.

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:06.601
Thank you so much.
I appreciate it.

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:08.133
Thank you for being here.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.100
We have time for one more.
We --

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.968
Right there. Come on.

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:13.501
Nice to see you.
-Hi.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:14.701
-What is your name
and where are you from?

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:16.334
-Victoria Ybarra.
I'm from California.

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:19.634
-Yeah, Victoria from California.

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:21.901
Alright.
The question is...

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:29.200
-A bar keeper?

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.434
[ Buzzer ]
-No.

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:32.434
We were looking
for a Spirit Airlines pilot.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:34.167
Sorry. Thank you
so much for being here.

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:36.200
-Unfortunately, no one
took home the prize tonight.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.467
We'll try again next week on

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:39.334
Tonight Show Audience
Trivia Night.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:41.901
Stick around. We'll be
right back with Matt Damon.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.200
Everybody, come on back.

